  "claimBoundary": "Strict zero-result pre-registration for a possible four-player milestone after the complete two-player gate. D-015 is an API direction, not a four-player product promise. D-071 requires the two-player milestone to pass and the four-player milestone to be explicitly activated before this campaign can open. The existing one-player prototype, two-player plan, Motion API shape, maxPlayers declaration, provider adapter limits, synthetic identity scenes, session rehearsals, vendor claims, or aggregate results cannot open the campaign or qualify four-player product quality. No complete two-player result, milestone activation, target, four-person tracker, room, larger safe play zone, participant quartet, calibration, accessible identity treatment, four-player join or recovery implementation, independent ground truth, runtime freeze adapter, camera collection, physical trial, result, qualification, selection, purchase, publication, maximum-player change, or product claim exists. The current living-room plan qualifies only a future measured one- and two-player zone; its exploratory four-player note is not room evidence. The current console lab remains configured for one player, and the current session-state-machine evidence stops at two players. Any later campaign must preserve sequential explicit joining, independent calibration, opaque session-local identities, number-pattern-shape-plus-color outlines, deterministic launcher and pause ownership, whole-game freeze after confirmed loss of any joined player, exact-original-roster silent reacquisition only, explicit full-roster recovery or roster reduction, independent per-player action attribution, zero aggregate rescue, safe measured separation, collision and emergency-stop truth, exposure-authoritative latency, complete adverse evidence, and strict privacy. A passing technical result would still require a separate owner decision before four-player product quality, room guidance, target selection, public compatibility, or a maximum-player promise changes.",
